          "title": "The Price of Greenwashing: Algorithmic Verification and Market Discipline using Conformal Machine Learning",
          "title_zh": "漂绿的代价：基于共形机器学习的算法验证与市场约束",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.02225v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2610.02225",
          "summary": "The paper fuses U.S. SEC financial fundamentals with facility-level EPA greenhouse-gas registries to build a mathematically guaranteed baseline of physical corporate emissions, then uses gradient boosting and Mondrian conformal prediction to quantify the gap with self-reported data as a Conformal-Weighted Continuous Divergence metric. It reports that this divergence has a significant negative relationship with subsequent Tobin's Q and ROA, which the authors read as markets pricing environmental deception.",
