          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.23242",
          "summary": "The paper proposes an end-to-end reinforcement learning method that learns continuation-value functions for two-timescale decision systems by combining a strictly convex potential of post-decision inventory with a learned convex residual, yielding a differentiable yet convex optimization layer for real-time execution. In an offline simulation using historical inventory and demand data from a large e-commerce retailer, it reduced total routing and transfer cost by 5.0% relative to a historical-production-system proxy.",
