          "title": "SoK: Formal Methods for Fact-Checking and Information Integrity",
          "title_zh": "SoK：面向事实核查与信息完整性的形式化方法",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.23239v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.23239",
          "summary": "This systematization of knowledge organizes 121 works on automated fact-checking by what is formalized rather than by pipeline stage, yielding five levels: the claim, the reasoning, the checking system, the information ecosystem, and the regulatory obligation. It finds that most relevant formal machinery already exists but was built for other domains, that the gap is widest for verifying the checking system itself, and that writing a claim in checkable form and correcting a published verdict lack stated correctness criteria.",
